  "notes": [
    "Grown in the high-altitude San Agustín area of Huila, Colombia, typically cultivated between 1,400 and 1,900 meters above sea level to encourage dense bean structure and complex sugars.",
    "Prepared using the fully washed process, which strips away the fruit pulp before drying to yield a clean, crisp cup with distinct citrus clarity.",
    "Best enjoyed via manual pour-over (such as a V60 or Chemex) or standard drip brewers to highlight the nuanced acidity and delicate maple sweetness of a light roast.",
    "Recommended brew ratio is 1:15 to 1:17 (about 15–16 grams of coffee per 250 grams of water) using water heated just off the boil to 200°F–205°F (93°C–96°C).",
    "Grind whole beans to a medium or medium-fine consistency immediately prior to brewing, and store the remaining beans in an opaque, airtight container in a cool, dry place."
  ],
